# PBI Push Workflow — Material Tracker Pro

Remote: https://github.com/Victor0870/PBI

## Default state on this machine

- `model.bim` uses **local** paths from `paths.local.json` (`D:\PBI\Data\...`)
- GitHub must always receive **remote** paths from `paths.remote.json` (`D:\Box\...`)

## When user requests push / đẩy lên github / commit and push

Run these steps **in order** — do not skip:

1. `.\scripts\switch-paths.ps1 -Mode Remote`
2. Verify `model.bim` contains `D:\Box\` and NOT `D:\PBI\Data\`
3. `git status` and `git diff` — review changes
4. `git add` relevant files + `git commit` (if changes exist)
5. `git push -u origin main` (or current branch)
6. **Always** run `.\scripts\switch-paths.ps1 -Mode Local`
7. Verify `model.bim` contains `D:\PBI\Data\` and NOT `D:\Box\`
8. Tell user push succeeded and local paths are restored

If step 5 fails, still run step 6 before reporting the error.

## Never

- Push while `model.bim` uses `D:\PBI\Data\` paths
- Forget to restore local paths after push
- Commit `paths.local.json` to Git

## First-time / path setup

- Remote paths: `paths.remote.json` (committed)
- Local paths: `paths.local.json` (gitignored)
- Switch script: `scripts/switch-paths.ps1` (calls `scripts/switch-paths.py`)

## Future: sales folder (Original)

When `Folder.Files` query is added to model, update both paths JSON files and re-run switch-paths.
